{
 "id": "REL-CMD-01",
 "criterion": "`callisto release` selects every package that has a publish target other than `none` and whose current version has no matching tag, or has a tag on the current commit while any of its operations is not observed already satisfied. For each one it runs the registry publishes, creates the git tag, and creates the GitHub release when `github-release` is a target. A tag on another commit marks the version released without contacting any provider."
}
{
 "id": "REL-CMD-02",
 "criterion": "When no package qualifies, `callisto release` prints `Nothing to release.` (JSON: `{\"nothingToRelease\": true}`), exits 0 and runs no command that publishes, pushes or creates anything."
}
{
 "id": "REL-CMD-03",
 "criterion": "`callisto release` runs on any branch, leaves HEAD on that branch, and records HEAD's commit as both `releaseSourceRevision` and `orchestrationRevision` in the receipt."
}
{
 "id": "REL-CMD-04",
 "criterion": "`callisto release --dry-run` prints a `Release plan:` header and each package as `<ecosystem/name> <version>` with its operations (a table on a colour terminal, indented lines otherwise) and performs no effect. This holds on a dirty worktree, without an `origin` remote, and in a workspace that needs the CI route. With `--format json` it prints the plan document, whose `digest` equals the receipt's `intentDigest` from a following `callisto release` on the same state; the document carries a sibling `diagnostics` array (e.g. an artifact owner selected without its product) when derivation raised any, and omits the field otherwise. `release plan`'s JSON output carries the same `diagnostics` array; the `--out` file it writes never does."
}
{
 "id": "REL-CMD-05",
 "criterion": "Without an `origin` push URL, `--dry-run` prints one stderr note that tag operations are unbound, and `callisto release` fails with E132 before any effect.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-CMD-06",
 "criterion": "A tracked modification or an untracked file not covered by `.gitignore` makes `callisto release` fail with E267 naming a clean worktree and the offending path, before any effect. Ignored files never count.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-CMD-07",
 "criterion": "Repeated `--package <ecosystem/name>` limits the run to the named packages, every distribution of each, and every package that shares a `fixed` or `linked` group with one of them."
}
{
 "id": "REL-CMD-08",
 "criterion": "A malformed `--package` value fails with `E227` and an unknown package with E102. A duplicate selection, a version whose release is complete, a package with no publish target, or a package whose current version is a `callisto snapshot` version fails with E169.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-CMD-09",
 "criterion": "Suppose a selected package has a runtime, optional or peer dependency on a publishable workspace package whose current version is untagged, and that package is not selected. Planning fails with E169 (\"select it too\") before any effect. A dependency whose current version is already tagged need not be selected.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-CMD-10",
 "criterion": "In a workspace with `[[release.artifact]]` slots or a napi/maturin platform package, `callisto release` fails with `E239` before any effect. The help names `release plan`, `release artifact-manifest` and `release execute`.",
 "is_error_case": true
}
{
 "id": "REL-CMD-11",
 "criterion": "On success, text output is `Released N package(s)`, followed by `; receipt saved to <path>` when `--receipt` is given, and JSON output is the receipt. A receipt file is written only to the `--receipt` path, never into the checkout, and an unwritable `--receipt` path fails the run before any effect."
}
{
 "id": "REL-CMD-12",
 "criterion": "`--format json` output of `release`, `release --dry-run`, `release plan`, `release execute` and `release artifact-manifest` goes through the same envelope every other command's JSON report uses: a top-level `schemaVersion`, `command` (the subcommand name) and `dryRun`, alongside that subcommand's own payload fields unchanged. The intent and artifact-manifest --out files, receipt --receipt file and version --emit-decision file use their durable document shape without command or dryRun wrapper fields."
}

